.TH "libnvme_alloc" 9 "libnvme_alloc" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvme_alloc \- Allocate zero-initialized memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void *" libnvme_alloc
.BI "(size_t len "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "len" 12
Number of bytes to allocate
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Allocates \fIlen\fP bytes of zero-initialized memory suitable for use by
libnvme APIs.
.SH "RETURN"
Pointer to the allocated memory on success, or NULL on failure.
